OL,3,GNEWSAPlans to stop HGV 'short-cut'
OL,4,Athrough town
OL,5,
OL,6,FA congestion charge for heavy goods
OL,7,Fvehicles is being considered to reduce
OL,8,Fthe number of trucks driving through an
OL,9,Friverside town.
OL,11,FHenley-on-Thames is frequently used as
OL,12,Fa short cut for trucks needing to cross
OL,13,Fthe river, but the town's narrow roads
OL,14,Fand local traffic can lead to severe
OL,15,Fcongestion.
OL,17,FThe council is now looking at options
OL,18,Fto remove some of the HGVs, including
OL,19,Fputting weight or size restrictions on
OL,20,Fthe town's bridge, physically changing
OL,21,Fthe road system and charging lorries
OL,22,Fcoming into the area.
OL,23,APub: 10-SepQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageB S Eng NewsC  Reg TVF Weather
